usage: generate.py [-h] [--model_path MODEL_PATH]
                   [--input_prompt INPUT_PROMPT]
                   [--compute_unit {All,CPUOnly,CPUAndGPU,CPUAndANE}]
                   [--length LENGTH] [--verbose VERBOSE] [--wait]
                   [--use-mlpackage] [--argmax] [--timingstats]

Load a CoreML modelpackage and generate some text.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --model_path MODEL_PATH
                        path to .mlpackage file
  --input_prompt INPUT_PROMPT
                        input prompt for the model
  --compute_unit {All,CPUOnly,CPUAndGPU,CPUAndANE}
                        compute unit
  --length LENGTH       number of new tokens to generate
  --verbose VERBOSE     print verbose logs
  --wait                wait for confirmation before loading the model (ie to
                        attach a debugger)
  --use-mlpackage       don't automatically generate a mlmodelc and use it.
                        dramatically slower but useful for debugging this
                        script.
  --argmax              use deterministic argmax instead of multinomial
                        sampling
  --timingstats         print verbose timing stats
